<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Volunteer Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917–1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Volunteer Army was the main anti-Bolshevik White army in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>, formed in late 1917 by generals Mikhail Alekseyev and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lavr-kornilov">Lavr Kornilov</a> and later led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Anton Denikin</a>. Based in the Kuban and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>, it fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> and local Soviet republics. It was defeated in 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/volunteer-army.jpg" alt="Volunteer Army" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thespoondragon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Volunteer_Army_Insignia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
